WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:21.813 --> 00:00:26.568
It's never clear whether Boo’ya
Moon was always there,

00:00:26.568 --> 00:00:30.864
whether it's a kind of alternate
world, an alternate reality.

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:32.949
Or whether it was actually created by

00:00:32.949 --> 00:00:36.745
the ferocity of Scott
Landon's imagination.

00:00:39.414 --> 00:00:42.834
Scott and Amanda both
have their dark sides.

00:00:43.835 --> 00:00:49.466
They're fragile. They experience life
in the world in a pretty intense way.

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:55.472
Boo'ya Moon is both really beautiful
and a very scary place.

00:00:56.431 --> 00:01:00.518
My character has to go to Boo'ya
Moon to draw my inspiration.

00:01:01.436 --> 00:01:03.438
And she does too.
She's struggling. And that's

00:01:03.438 --> 00:01:05.815
the place that she goes to heal.

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:12.906
Amanda is the one that really
understands both worlds.

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:17.619
She really can experience what Scott's
created in a very particular way,

00:01:17.619 --> 00:01:22.665
and can navigate this reality with
this world of fiction

00:01:22.665 --> 00:01:23.833
and of this fantasy.

00:01:39.182 --> 00:01:41.226
Missus, I thought we
had an agreement.

00:01:42.352 --> 00:01:44.979
Seems like you don't get how
serious this business is,

00:01:44.979 --> 00:01:47.065
although I'd thought a dead crow
in the mailbox would be pretty

00:01:47.065 --> 00:01:48.691
hard to misunderstand.

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:52.445
I'll be seein' ya.

00:01:56.074 --> 00:01:57.534
F*** you, Jimmy.

00:01:58.701 --> 00:02:01.412
Now, missus, that isn't a bit nice.

